{
  "_note": "Recorded foley for the Farmhouse, played in place of the synthesized takes. One file is one whole sound. steps: a walk across a ceiling, heard from the room below (about six seconds). knock: one knuckle on a wooden table, heard from under it. creak: a floorboard or a hinge. floor: boards taking weight under a table. house: one long groan of old timber. latch: an iron cellar latch lifting and dropping. breath: one slow breath close to a microphone. Name the files here, 2 to 4 of each; plain file names only. scratch: nails dragged slowly along the underside of a wooden table, three or four strokes. knocks, light, near, stairs, door, shut, chair, thud, nails, drag, gasp, rattle, glass, chime are the demon's sounds (game.js playSfx; audio.js A.rec places each one); match is the struck match on the title, snuff a candle going out, slam the planchette landing hard. The table's props (2026-10-08, game.js the props package): salt-tip, napkin, fork-scrape, pen-roll, keys, mug-turn, glasses-open, matches-roll, glass-crack, glass-break, flies, phone-ring, remote-click, tv-on, each placed where its prop sits on the table (tv-on in the room to the left). An entry may be { file, gain }: the gain multiplies that take wherever it plays (the phone's ring and the television are loud, the napkin and the mug near silence), measured against the knock and the latch. The looks' kinds (cat-clock, micro-keys, micro-done, tv-on, static, ceiling, house-far, under) and the props' (salt-tip to remote-click) are the 2026-10-08 ElevenLabs takes, none heard by Pierce yet; an entry may be { file, gain }.",
